node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
# Never commit real credentials. The previous version shipped an OAuth client
# secret in lib/auth.js; this build uses the OAuth implicit flow, which has no
# token-exchange step and therefore no secret to leak.
secrets.json
.env

# Generated by tools/make-preview.mjs. Regenerate rather than edit.
preview.html

# Generated by tools/make-bisect.mjs — throwaway diagnostic extension folders.
tools/bisect/

.benchlabs/


# Failure evidence: the smoke tool's scene (screenshot, DOM, console,
# trace) and the self-integrity gate's shard manifest.
.smoke-failure.*
.smoke-trace.zip
.ci-manifest.json

# ---- SCRATCH ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# THE CONVENTION: throwaway verification lives in /.scratch/. One directory,
# one rule, nothing to remember.
#
# WHY IT IS A DIRECTORY AND NOT A PREFIX LIST (round 9, H-4). This section
# used to carry six patterns — /.shot.mjs, /.shot2.mjs, /.shot-cp.mjs,
# /.probe*.mjs, /.probe-*.mjs, .shot*.png — each added when someone invented
# a new name. Eleven `.v-*.mjs` probes then shipped inside the extension
# package, because the list did not anticipate a twelfth prefix and a
# leading-dot file is invisible in a casual `ls`. A rule that has to be
# extended every session is a rule that will be missed; a directory cannot be
# misspelled into the repo.
#
# THE LEGACY PREFIXES ARE COLLAPSED (round 10, L-23). Six named patterns were
# left behind last round "so an older working copy does not suddenly start
# offering its scratch for commit" — but keeping a list is what failed twice:
# /.v-*.mjs did not match .v9-*, and the round before that no pattern matched
# .v-* at all. Two shapes replace all six, and neither can be misspelled into
# the repo:
#
#   /.scratch/          where throwaway verification belongs
#   /.*.mjs, /.*.png    any leading-dot script or shot at the ROOT
#
# Root-level only (the leading slash), so a legitimate dotfile deeper in the
# tree is unaffected. No tracked file matches either pattern — verified with
# `git ls-files | grep '^\.'` — so nothing already committed is hidden by
# this, which is the failure mode a broad ignore rule can otherwise cause.
/.scratch/
/.*.mjs
/.*.png
